    3.02 Daily Checks           ATTENTION — For your safety:
                                Before commencing any repair or inspection, isolate
    • Visual checks of all joints and for signs of leakage of product, power to pump and drive motor, depressurize, drain
     flushing liquid (if used). and isolated pipework. 
    • Listen for any unusual noises                    
    • Check for any unusual vibration or temperature changes. Size Bolt Torque
    • If minor problems are identified these should be rectified at
                                  040  M5   2.25Nm     
     the end of the shift and if major they should be attended to
     immediately.                 080  M6   6.8Nm      
    3.03 Weekly Checks            200  M8   13.5Nm     
    • As Daily Checks.            370  M8   13.5Nm     
    • Remove end cover of pump and inspect Impeller for signs of
                                  End cover and Body Bolt Torque
     damage or wear. Repair or replace as necessary.   
    3.04 Monthly Checks      5.01 End cover            
                             Before removing the end cover, ensure the pump &amp; drive are
    • As Weekly Checks.                                
                             isolated; the pump is cool enough to safely touch, drained of any
    • Visually check Impeller for damage or wear and seal housing fluids (take special care with hazardous fluids) and ensure that
     for leaks.              pump and seal flushing systems are isolated and depressurized.
